// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// specs/0052 W1 — THE SIBERIA FRAME'S DEM, AS A REGION BUNDLE.
//
// D-1 (Greg, 2026-09-06): A REGION IS A SEAM. Siberia Bowl and the Palisades
// cliff band are the west end of one mountain, but their data is NOT in the
// first load: this module is fetched on approach and handed to ground.mjs's
// `registerFrameDem()` hook (W2R, specs/0052 §6). Nothing in the shipped
// red-dog graph imports it. That is the whole point, and it is also why
// check 1 on red-dog is byte-identical with this file sitting on disk: the
// router's fast path is `if (!RESIDENT.length) return z`, and in the first
// load RESIDENT is empty.
//
// WHAT IS IN HERE, AND WHAT IS NOT
//
//   DEM_TIGHT   1400 m frame at its FULL NATIVE 1024^2 (1.3672 m/px), copied
//               BYTE FOR BYTE out of runs/siberia-palisades-A-raw-01/scene/
//               dem-data.mjs. Not re-baked, not re-quantised, not decimated —
//               the same base64 the siberia world ships today, so the merged
//               router reads the same 3DEP samples siberia's own check 1
//               hashed (`b9b509afd3e38d29`).
//
//   DEM_WIDE    DELIBERATELY ABSENT — 0052 §1.4 / D-9. `DEM_UP_WIDE`
//               (dem-upper.mjs, 3600 m @ 7.031 m/px) covers 100 % of siberia's
//               crop box with >= 233 m of margin on the tight frame and
//               >= 292 m on CORE, and the two surrounds agree to a mean |dz|
//               of 0.096 m over their 2,797 x 3,184 m overlap (0052 S8). It is
//               worth a MEASURED 190,185 B of brotli (GATE-0052-W0 §6), and
//               the surround it buys is ground the region's own tight frame
//               already answers for everywhere a player can stand.
//
// THE FRAME IS DECLARED, NOT DERIVED HERE. This module states siberia's own
// ORIGIN_LAT / ORIGIN_LON / Z_DATUM — the three numbers its bundle's
// layout.mjs states — and NOTHING ELSE about the map. ground.mjs's
// `registerFrameDem()` derives ox/oy/scale/dz against the REFERENCE frame it
// already holds (frames.mjs `REF`, whose scale W0 fixed), so there is exactly
// ONE place in the world that knows how two frames relate and this file is not
// it. Consequence: this module imports nothing at all, which is what lets W2R
// serve it from `r/<pin8>/regions/siberia/` without a specifier to rewrite.
//
// Row 0 = SOUTH edge, +x east. Values are DECIMETRES relative to
// z0 = 2366.0 m ASL (the Siberia Express BASE terminal; 3DEP reads 2366.3 m at
// the OSM end node). World frame: ENU ground metres about 39.18375,-120.26625
// (dem-tight/aerial.jpg centre), x = (merc_x - merc_x0)*cos(lat0),
// y = (merc_y - merc_y0)*cos(lat0).
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

/** siberia's own vertical datum, m ASL. `DEM_TIGHT`'s values are relative to it. */
export const DEM_Z0 = 2366.0;

/** siberia's own horizontal origin, verbatim from that bundle's layout.mjs
 *  (`ORIGIN_LAT`, `ORIGIN_LON`, `Z_DATUM`). ground.mjs turns these three into
 *  the frame-to-reference map; see registerFrameDem(). */
export const ORIGIN = { lat: 39.18375, lon: -120.26625, z0: DEM_Z0 };

// 1400 m frame, ASL 2317.2..2699.0 — verbatim from the siberia bundle.
export const DEM_TIGHT = { span: 1400.0, n: 1024, ox: -0.00, oy: 0.00, b64: "" };

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// THE HANDOFF. `grids` is COARSEST FIRST, the same order ground.mjs's own DEM
// stack is written in, and each entry is the ENCODED grid object: ground.mjs
// decodes it with the same `decode()` every other frame goes through, so the
// 0051 §6.4 discipline (null the b64 source string once the Int16Array is
// filled) applies to this frame too and is written in exactly one place.
//
// `fade` is the cross-fade in metres of frame inset, matching the 70 m every
// other frame in the stack uses; `core` is this region's playable box in
// FRAME-LOCAL metres (siberia layout.mjs `CORE`), which is what W2R's trigger
// polygon and the 0051 void fence want once ground.mjs has mapped it.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
export const SIBERIA_FRAME_DEM = {
  id: 'siberia',
  origin: ORIGIN,
  grids: [DEM_TIGHT],
  fade: 70,
  core: { x0: -640, x1: 850, y0: -470, y1: 540 },
};

export default SIBERIA_FRAME_DEM;
